# What does a positive test mean?
subtitle: "Guess how many of 108 positive tests are real, and see why a 90 % accurate test is right only about one time in twelve."
tags: ["probability","disease testing","bayes theorem","medical diagnosis","accuracy paradox","false positives"]
teaches: ["concepts/bayes-theorem","concepts/false-positive-rate","concepts/conditional-probability","methods/interpreting-test-results"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Sadachbia | a lively quiz host with a statistical twist; playful, clear","take":"lines"}

## What does a positive test mean?
    population all fit.h 350 fit.w 880 fit.x 60 fit.y 370 count 100 states.healthy 99 states.sick 1 order spread labels.healthy healthy labels.sick sick hidden true
    population pos fit top count 108 states.healthy 99 states.sick 9 order rows labels.healthy "false alarm" labels.sick sick hidden true

If a test is ninety percent accurate and you test positive, how likely are you to be sick? Say one person in a hundred has the disease.
    draw all

And the test is right nine times in ten: it finds nine in ten of the sick, and it clears nine in ten of the healthy.
    text cue2 "Test right 9 in 10" x 500 y 320 font_size 34

    erase all

Now test a thousand people. A hundred and eight of them test positive.
    text cue3 "108 test positive" x 500 y 265 font_size 34

    ask "Of these hundred and eight, how many do you think really have the disease? Mark how many are sick." on pos_sick store s default "90" tolerance 0.05
        right: You said {s}. Right: only {s.true}.
        wrong: You said {s}. Only {s.true} have it; the rest are false alarms.

Of the thousand, only ten have the disease, and the test finds nine of them.
    highlight pos_sick

But nine hundred and ninety are healthy, and one in ten of them is flagged anyway: ninety-nine false alarms.
    highlight pos_healthy

    erase cue2 cue3

So a positive result means about an eight percent chance of having the disease, not ninety. That is why a positive screen is usually followed by a second test.
    text result "9 of 108 ≈ 8 %" x 500 y 290 font_size 48
